<div style="margin-left:72pt;width:468pt"><p style="font:10pt Times New Roman;margin-top:6pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-right:-6.5pt">Consolidated total 2Q 2026 revenues were $1,424 (14.3%) lower than in 2Q 2025, with 1H 2026 revenues $2,411 (12.3%) lower than in 1H 2025. The lower sales in comparison with the prior year&#8217;s periods were primarily the result of a lack of sales to UTMD&#8217;s two previously largest customers, representing a combined $1,065 loss in 2Q 2025 sales, which was 75% of the 2Q decline; and representing a combined $1,923 loss in 1H 2025 sales, which was 80% of the 1H decline. The total 2025 sales to these two former customers were $2,889, which UTMD planned to recover in sales of new products in 2026, mainly to other biopharma OEM customers. Sales to other biopharma new customers were just $211 in 1H 2026, a slower than expected gain. Additional period-to-period sales comparisons follow below.</p>
<p style="font:10pt Times New Roman;margin-top:6pt;margin-bottom:0pt">UTMD&#8217;s profit margins compared to those of the prior year&#8217;s same periods follow:</p>
